-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[28] = {
[14000]={"<rgb=#00FF00>¡Los primeros asaltantes han sido derrotados! Reagrupa y consulta con el Segundo vigilante Heathstraw</rgb>","'¡Bree está a salvo! Nos has prestado un gran servicio al ayudar en la causa. Podría haber aguantado un poco, pero ese semiorco con Bill Helechal y Harry Madreselva sin duda me habrían derrotado si hubiera estado solo. Te agradezco enormemente tu ayuda.'","El Segundo vigilante Heathstraw está justo fuera de El Poney Pisador. Desea hablar contigo sobre el éxito de hoy.","'A menudo, durante escaramuzas como esta, encontrarás que tienes otros aliados, como yo, que te ayudan en la batalla. En algunos casos, si esos aliados caen, perderás la escaramuza.'","Habla con el Segundo vigilante Heathstraw","'Cuando tomaste la Puerta Sur, atravesaste y reclamaste los baluartes enemigos. Aquí defendemos el Poney Pisador y los baluartes que hemos reclamado, mientras el enemigo viene hacia nosotros para intentar tomarlos.'","'Te agradezco de nuevo tu ayuda al liberar Bree. Pasará mucho tiempo antes de que se olvide lo que has hecho.'","'Siempre puedes comprar recompensas y entrenar a tu Soldado en cualquiera de los Campamentos de Escaramuza del mundo.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Los terceros asaltantes han sido derrotados. Dríthlorz ha sido vencido, y Bree es libre una vez más</rgb>","El Segundo vigilante Heathstraw está justo fuera del Poney Pisador. Desea comentar su plan contigo.","Tutorial: Defensa del Poney Pisador","Derrota a los últimos asaltantes y a Dríthlorz","'Es importante asegurarse de que tu soldado está bien entrenado para el rol que quieres que cumpla. Presta atención a los demás miembros de tu comunidad, a sus habilidades y a qué soldados convocarán.'","El enemigo está lanzando su ataque final contra El Poney Pisador. Ayuda al Segundo vigilante Heathstraw a defenderlo","El Segundo vigilante Heathstraw está justo fuera del Poney Pisador. Desea comentar contigo algunos detalles finales.","'Me alegra ver que has regresado, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Hemos logrado llegar a El Poney Pisador en tu ausencia y hemos conseguido mantenerlo, pero temo que no resistiremos mucho más. Los forajidos vienen contra nosotros con una ferocidad que no puedo igualar. Me alegra tenerte de nuevo a mi lado.'","Compra el rasgo de Rol de Guerrero a Will, luego habla con Tom para asignarlo, y después usa tu habilidad para invocar a tu Guerrero","El enemigo está atacando el Poney Pisador. Ayuda al Segundo vigilante Heathstraw a defenderlo.","El Segundo vigilante Heathstraw está justo fuera del Poney Pisador. Desea hablar contigo.","'Hay una gran cantidad y variedad de recompensas disponibles por ayudar a los Pueblos Libres a luchar contra el Enemigo.'","'Ese orco era uno de los lugartenientes de los que hablaba. Hiciste bien en derrotarlo.'","<rgb=#FF0000>El enemigo se aproxima desde el oeste</rgb>","<rgb=#00FF00>¡Los segundos asaltantes han sido derrotados! Reagrupa y consulta con el Segundo vigilante Heathstraw</rgb>","Will y Tom están fuera del Poney Pisador. Quieren ayudarte a mejorar a tu soldado permitiéndote comprar y asignar un rasgo de rol para convertirlo en guerrero.","Derrota a los segundos asaltantes","'A menudo sabemos poco sobre las fuerzas enemigas o de dónde pueden venir exactamente. Tras explorar, sé que nos enfrentamos a forajidos, semiorcos y lobos de diversa habilidad y fuerza. Pero no sé qué combinación de ellos podría atacarnos en cualquier momento. Mantente en guardia y prepárate para ajustar tu defensa en cualquier momento para resistir mejor los asaltos enemigos.'","'Asegurarte de que tu soldado está entrenado para complementar tus propias habilidades y las de tu comunidad es crucial para superar los desafíos de cada Escaramuza contra el enemigo.'","Los habitantes de Bree han pasado la ocupación atrincherados dentro del Poney Pisador. Enfurecidos por su levantamiento, los bandidos han decidido quemarlos....","Derrota a los primeros asaltantes"},
[14001]={"Tutorial: First Steps in the Ettenmoors","You have arrived at Ost Ringdyr","'To the east, behind the foliage and stones, there is a path that leads to the keep of Ost Ringdyr. We keep a relic of power within those walls.\
\
'I want you to travel there to see why we fight. I have provided you with a map showing a quick path back here to Glân Vraig. Go now with haste and return by way of the map, so that I know you are prepared for the battle to come.\
\
'Travel along that path to the east and stay close to cliffside so you do not fall down into the proper battlefield.'","Use the skill <rgb=#FFFF00>Return to Glân Vraig</rgb>","Travel out of Glân Vraig by the path along the cliffside to the east of Captain-General Tordúr and make your way to Ost Ringdyr.","'It is good to know that there are those like you, willing to come and fight for this land. We will remain resolute in this battle. The armies of Angmar will not press into the south, and it is by our force of arms combined that we shall see this through.\
\
'You are prepared as best as I can see. Go forth.'","'Have you made use of your map and what it taught you?'\
\
Use the skill <rgb=#FFFF00>Return to Glân Vraig</rgb>.","You have discovered the keep of Ost Ringdyr. You should now use the skill <rgb=#FFFF00>Return to Glân Vraig</rgb> to quickly return to the main encampment.","You have returned to Glân Vraig","Arrive at Ost Ringdyr","You have returned to Glân Vraig. Speak with Captain-General Tordúr and let him know that you are prepared to fight in the battle for the Ettenmoors.","You are nearly prepared for battle, but the Captain-General has one more task for you before he sends you into the fray."},
[14010]={"Talk to Durglob","Tutorial: Learning the Tools","Uglash has implored you to return to your trainers and learn how better to equip yourself for the battles to come.","Now that you have equipped some traits, speak with the corruptions trainer to learn more about corruptions in Monster Play.","'Return to your trainers. They can help you fight without getting squashed like an insignificant slug. Hurry! The war doesn't stop just because you aren't ready for it.'","Uglash has asked you to return to your trainers and learn more about what it takes to become a true soldier in the war against the Free Peoples.\
\
The trainers are back where you started your life as an Orc.","'Good! You are still alive! Hopefully you've learned a thing or two about how to keep yourself from being meat for the slugs. \
\
'There are many things that need to be done to win this war. Speak with the soldiers around the totem behind me to help in the war-effort. You can also view the state of the war in the tent up on the hill. Some of the warriors up there may have things for you to do from time to time as well.\
\
'Now quit staring with that vacant look in your eyes and get out there and fight!'","Now that you have learned how to best equip yourself in Monster Play, speak with Uglash again for final instructions.","'Well, it's about time someone knocked some sense into you! Now shut your gob and pay attention! This isn't some weak-armed, sunken-chest game we are playing out here.\
\
'Good. Now, talk to me again if you wish to purchase traits, then speak with the Corruptor.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>In Monster Play, you will earn </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Infamy</rgb><rgb=#00FF00> and </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Commendations</rgb><rgb=#00FF00> by defeating the Free Peoples. As you accrue </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Infamy</rgb><rgb=#00FF00>, your rank (level) will increase, granting you access to additional skills, traits, and characteristics.  You can then purchase these from your trainer with </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Commendations.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Speak with the trainer again if you wish to purchase additional skills and traits.</rgb>","'Can I help you? No? Great.\
\
'Oh, you're still here?  Well then, if you purchased some traits from your trainer, then you can equip them with me.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00> You have a corruption ready to be equipped. To equip traits and corruptions speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections.</rgb>","Talk to Uglash to finish the tutorial","Having spoken with Dagalúr, you should now talk to the Corruptor to learn about traits.","Return to your trainers and learn how to improve your skills","'So you think you are smart enough to understand the concept of trade-offs?  Then you are a bigger fool than most give you credit for. Corruptions will grant you incredible powers, but you can only use a handful at a time.  Choose wisely.'\
\
'Uglash wishes to speak with you again.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00> Corruptions offer the players the ability to raise certain stats in exchange for lowering other ones. This is available for players who wish to specialize even further than their Monster Player class allows. </rgb>","Talk to Ashrokil, the Corruptor of Gramsfoot"},
[14011]={"'Welcome, mistress. Your presence in this war-torn land is welcome. The filth that fights in the Lord's name falter at every turn. Perhaps with our hand to guide them we will turn the tide and finally force our way south to discover the hidden Elven stronghold. Though it is beneath you, your first task is to meet with War-tyrant Akulhún. You will find him behind you shouting incessantly in the shadow of the totems. Be warned, he has a temper.'","'Well... well... a new pup fresh from a litter in the mires of Angmar. Finally ready to wet your pelt with the blood of our enemies? Good, bare your teeth. Gird your loins. Your first task is to meet the War-tyrant. Akulhún stands before the totems near the bonfires. Make your way to him and report your arrival.\
\
'Go now. Make the pack proud.'","'Here's a specimen ready for battle! Now, if only I could get the Lord of Angmar to recall the damned emissary he's sent here. Welcome to the front!'","You are directed to speak with War-tyrant Akulhún, the leader of the forces in Gramsfoot. He awaits you at the totems and bonfires down the hill near the exit into the Ettenmoors proper.","Tutorial: Out of Angmar","Welcome to the Ettenmoors! It is time to learn your way around. Follow your orders and prepare to meet the enemy outside of the encampment at Gramsfoot!","'You have just been hatched, broodling, but already you must play an important role. Mordirith sends you here to aid in the war against the Free Peoples. We have no time to waste. You must now get your feet wet. All of them.\
\
'Seek out the War-tyrant Akulhún near the totems and bonfires. He is the ultimate leader in the Ettenmoors and will give you your orders!'","'Pay attention, maggot! You are nothing! A speck. I don't know why Mordirith sent you here, other than to die like the rest! Ha! You need to make an impression or, at least an introduction. Make your way to the totems surrounded by bonfires. Find War-tyrant Akulhún and report in.\
\
'Now, get out of my face. You sicken me.'"},
[14015]={"Malavin, el emisario de Angmar, te indicó que regresaras al lugar donde comenzaste tu viaje en las Landas de Etten para hablar con el corruptor allí.","Malavan sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Lenathron the corruptor.","'Greetings, broodling. Freshly arrived and visited the emissary? Allow me to assist you. I can aid in your survival and skill in the coming battles.'\
\
The spider swipes at you.\
\
'Consider this a lesson. Speak with me again to continue your lessons.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>To equip traits and Corruptions speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and Corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections.</rgb>","'Now that you have chosen a clan you must learn how to further strengthen and enhance yourself so that you are more than a distraction against the enemy. Return to the location you arrived and speak with Zagfra. They will show you the power that corruption can provide.'","Return to your spawning den. Speak with Lenathron the Corruptor.","Tutorial: El Poder de la Corrupción"},
[14016]={"'Always good to see the real warriors here in the Ettenmoors. I can help you survive, slaughter, even thrive in this war. You will need my help.'\
\
The Orc swipes at you.\
\
'Consider this a lesson. Speak with me again to continue your lessons.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00> After completing this quest, you will have your first corruption. To equip traits and Corruptions speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and Corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections. </rgb>","Malavin, el emisario de Angmar, te indicó que regresaras al lugar donde comenzaste tu viaje en las Landas de Etten para hablar con el corruptor allí.","Tutorial: El Poder de la Corrupción","'Now that you have chosen a clan, you must learn how to further strengthen and enhance yourself so that you are more than a distraction against the enemy. Return to the location you arrived and speak with Ashrokil. They will show you the power that corruption can provide.'","Return to your spawning den. Speak with Ashrokil the Corruptor.","Malavan sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Ashrokil the corruptor."},
[14017]={"Malavin, el emisario de Angmar, te indicó que regresaras al lugar donde comenzaste tu viaje en las Landas de Etten para hablar con el corruptor allí.","Malavan sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Zagfra the Corruptor.","'Now that you have chosen a clan, you must learn how to further strengthen and enhance yourself so that you are more than a distraction against the enemy. Return to the location you arrived and speak with Zagfra. They will show you the power that corruption can provide.'","'The emissary told me she would send the newest pups my way. Well pup, I am here to enhance your ability to survive and slaughter in this unforgiving land.'\
\
The Warg swipes at you.\
\
'Consider this a lesson. Speak with me again to continue your lessons.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>After completing this quest your will have your first corruption. To equip traits and Corruptions, speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and Corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections. </rgb>","Return to your spawning den. Speak with Zagfra the Corruptor.","Tutorial: El Poder de la Corrupción"},
[14018]={"Malavin, el emisario de Angmar, te indicó que regresaras al lugar donde comenzaste tu viaje en las Landas de Etten para hablar con el corruptor allí.","'Familiarizarte con los distintos clanes es el primer paso para curtirte en el campo de batalla. Para continuar con tu preparación, regresa a la puerta principal y habla con Cinaid. Él te dará más instrucciones y te preparará para la batalla que se avecina.\
\
'Una vez más, hermana, bienvenida a la lucha. Que los verdaderos hijos les muestren a estas criaturas inferiores cómo se debe pelear una guerra.'","'Me alegra verte aún aquí, señora de la oscuridad. Las lecciones que tengo para enseñarte son muchas y importantes. Te serán de gran ayuda en esta tierra fétida.'\
\
Hace una pausa por un momento.\
\
'Creo que es hora de prepararte como corresponde.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Al completar esta misión, obtendrás tu primera corrupción. Para equipar rasgos y corrupciones, habla nuevamente con el Corruptor. Selecciona los rasgos y corrupciones disponibles de la lista y arrástralos a los espacios vacíos de rasgos. Cuando termines, confirma tus selecciones.</rgb>","Malavin te indicó que regresaras con Cinaid, cerca de la puerta principal de Gramsfoot. Él te ayudará a seguir preparándote para luchar en las Landas de Etten.","Tutorial: El Poder de la Corrupción"},
[14019]={"'You have just been hatched, broodling, but already you must play an important role. Mordirith has sent you here to aid in the war against the Free Peoples. We have no time to waste. You must go get your feet wet now, all of them.\
\
'Head down the hill and out the front gate and speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz. He will have orders for you. We must share our web with interesting allies to be victorious. Now go!'","'What are you doing here, recruit? You aren't ready to step foot out here! Why do they keep sending me fodder? I need trained soldiers. Get back in the base and learn something before a Burglar stealth kills you!\
\
'Return to the camp now and speak with Uglash! Come back to me when you've learned a thing or two about fighting out here.'","Return to safety and speak with Uglash","Tutorial: Spinning the Web","Tolothdal has ordered you to get into the fight already. She wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south.  Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.","Get back to safety","'Pitiful fool. \
\
'You've passed the first test. You follow orders blindly even when it means certain death. Well done.  Now let us see if you can learn more obvious thoughts like \\qthe Orc with the bigger sword wins.\\q'","Get your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz","You are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the camp to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.","Having entered the Ettenmoors as a spider, you need to learn your way around. Follow your orders and do not get yourself killed by the Free Peoples who lurk around every corner."},
[14020]={"'You have just been hatched, broodling, but already you must play an important role. Mordirith has sent you here to aid in the war against the Free Peoples. We have no time to waste. You must go get your feet wet now, all of them.\
\
'Head down the hill and out the front gate and speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz. He will have orders for you. We must share our web with interesting allies to be victorious. Now go!'","Return to safety and speak with Uglash","Tutorial: Spinning the Web","Tolothdal has ordered you to get into the fight already. She wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.","'What are you doing here, recruit? You aren't ready to step foot out here! Why do they keep sending me fodder? I need trained soldiers. Get back in the camp and learn something before a Burglar stealth kills you!\
\
Return to the camp now and speak with Uglash! Come back to me when you've learned a thing or two about fighting out here.'","Get back to safety","Get your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz","You are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the base to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.","Having entered the Ettenmoors as a spider, you need to learn your way around. Follow your orders and do not get yourself killed by the Free Peoples who lurk around every corner.","'Pitiful fool.\
\
'You've passed the first test. You follow orders blindly even when it means certain death. Well done. Now let us see if you can learn more obvious thoughts like \\qthe Orc with the bigger sword wins.\\q'"},
[14022]={"'Tu Soldado es un aliado poderoso en la lucha contra la oscuridad que avanza. Te ayudará enormemente en tus batallas contra el Enemigo.'","'Usa la habilidad que te enseñó el cuerno para convocar a un Soldado de los Pueblos Libres. No sobrevivirás si intentas asaltar las puertas de Bree tú ${PLAYERNAME:solo[m]|sola[f]}.'","'Ve a descansar. Hoy has hecho mucho bien por el mundo. Mañana hará falta más, pero por esta noche, disfruta del respiro.'","'Usa el cuerno, y te enseñará cómo convocar a un Soldado para que se una a ti en tu Escaramuza contra el enemigo.'","<rgb=#00FF00>La Puerta Sur de Bree ha pasado a tu control. El siguiente lugar importante es la Casa de Subastas justo delante</rgb>","La habilidad de Soldado está en tu Panel de Habilidades, en la sección de Escaramuza. Necesitarás usarla para invocar a un Soldado que te ayude.","La bandera está en la Puerta Sur de Bree. Para reclamar este Punto de Control necesitas usar la bandera.","Toma el control de la Casa de Subastas de Bree","<rgb=#00FF00>Has tomado el control de la Casa de Subastas</rgb>","Toma el control de la casa de Bill Helechal y derrota a Dríthlorz","Usa el cuerno para aprender a llamar a un Soldado","Usa tu nueva habilidad para convocar a un Soldado","Mientras los Montaraces del Norte estaban distraídos en el Sur, unos bandidos aprovecharon la oportunidad para arrebatar el control de Bree....","El Segundo vigilante Heathstraw está en su campamento, justo fuera de la Puerta Sur de Bree. Está esperando a que informes.","El Segundo vigilante Heathstraw está justo fuera de la casa de Bill Helechal. Desea hablar contigo sobre vuestra victoria.","Un Soldado de los Pueblos Libres aparece para ayudarte en tu Escaramuza contra el Enemigo.","'La Puerta Sur debe tomarse primero. Si no está bajo nuestro control, no podemos esperar avanzar más dentro de Bree.'","Usar el cuerno te ha enseñado la habilidad necesaria para llamar a un Soldado en una Escaramuza.","Tutorial: Robo y Travesuras","'No pensé que la ayuda llegaría tan rápido, pero me alegra ver que así ha sido. Me temo que la situación ahora mismo no es muy buena. Unos bandidos, dejados entrar por Bill Helechal y Harry Madreselva, han tomado gran parte de Bree.'","El Segundo vigilante Heathstraw está en su campamento, justo fuera de la Puerta Sur de Bree. Desea comentar contigo su plan para recuperar la ciudad.","'Los líderes de las fuerzas enemigas suelen ser criaturas astutas y poderosas. No deben tomarse a la ligera.'","El cuerno está sobre una caja junto al Segundo vigilante Heathstraw. Necesitarás usarlo para aprender a convocar a un Soldado al combate.","La Puerta Sur está justo al norte del campamento del Segundo vigilante Heathstraw. Necesitarás eliminar a todos los enemigos alrededor de la bandera para reclamarla.","'Has hecho un gran trabajo aquí hoy, ${PLAYER}. Aún queda mucho por hacer, pero por hoy, descansemos y curémonos.'","La Casa de Subastas está al norte de la Puerta Sur de Bree. Los enemigos deben ser eliminados y la bandera utilizada para tomar este punto.","Usa la bandera para reclamar la Puerta Sur","<rgb=#00FF00>Dríthlorz ha sido derrotado y la casa de Bill Helechal está asegurada. Bree aún no es libre, pero se ha avanzado mucho</rgb>","Toma el control de la Puerta Sur de Bree","Informa de tu éxito al Segundo vigilante Heathstraw","'A menudo, el enemigo no estará contento por perder un lugar importante. Ten cuidado... pueden lanzar un contraataque para intentar recuperarlo.'","Los monstruos de la Puerta Sur han sido eliminados. Usa la bandera para reclamar el Punto de Control.","Habla con el Segundo vigilante Heathstraw","La casa de Bill Helechal está al este de la Casa de Subastas. Debéis derrotar a Dríthlorz y sus aliados y usar la bandera para recuperar esta parte de Bree."},
[14023]={"Return to safety and speak with Uglash","Having entered the Ettenmoors as a Warg, you need to learn your way around. Follow your orders and do not get yourself killed by the Free Peoples who lurk around every corner.","'What are you doing here, recruit? You aren't ready to step foot out here! Why do they keep sending me fodder? I need trained soldiers. Get back in the camp and learn something before a Burglar stealth kills you!\
\
'Return to the camp now and speak with Uglash! Come back to me when you've learned a thing or two about fighting out here.'","Get your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz","Get back to safety","Tutorial: Thrown to the Wargs","You are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the base to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.","Morsûm has ordered you to get into the fight already. He wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.","'Pitiful fool.\
\
'You've passed the first test. You follow orders blindly even when it means certain death. Well done. Now let us see if you can learn more obvious thoughts like \\qthe Orc with the bigger sword wins.\\q'","'Pay attention, pup! You are nothing, a speck. I don't know why Mordirith sent you here, but perhaps you can help. Head out the front gate to the South and get in the fray. Speak to Chief Guard Duthúrz out at the first camp-site. He will have work for you.\
\
'Get out of my face. You sicken me.'"},
